[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.100]   Ladies and gentlemen, thank you for standing by, and welcome to Constellium's Second
[00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.560]   Quarter 2020 results call.
[00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:12.580]   At this time, all participants are in a listen-only mode.
[00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:17.240]   Later, we will conduct a question and answer session, and instructions will follow at that
[00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.240]   time.
[00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.360]   If anyone should require assistance during the conference, please press star zero on
[00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:24.360]   your touch-tone telephone.
[00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.040]   As a reminder, this conference call may be recorded.
[00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:32.220]   I would now like to turn the conference over to your host today, Mr. Ryan Wendtling,
[00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.940]   Director of Investor Relations.
[00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:36.800]   Sir, please go ahead.
[00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:37.800]   Thank you, operator.
[00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.020]   I would like to welcome everyone to our Second Quarter 2020 earnings call.
[00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:46.700]   On the call today are our Chief Executive Officer, Jean-Marc Germain, and our Chief
[00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.640]   Financial Officer, Peter Maas.
[00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.860]   After the presentation, we will have a Q&A session.
[00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:57.020]   A copy of the slide presentation for today's call is available on our website at Constellium.com
[00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:59.060]   and today's call is being recorded.
[00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:04.260]   Before we begin, I would like to encourage everyone to visit the company's website and
[00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:07.360]   take a look at our recent filings.
[00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:11.360]   Today's call may include forward-looking statements within the meaning of the Private
[00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:14.760]   Securities Litigation Reform Act of 1995.
[00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:18.580]   Such statements include statements regarding the company's anticipated financial and operating
[00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:25.100]   performance, future events and expectations, and may involve known and unknown risks and
[00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.100]   uncertainties.
[00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:29.260]   Please refer a summary of specific risk factors that could cause results different
[00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:32.960]   materially from those expressed in the forward-looking statements.
[00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:36.840]   Please refer to the factors presented under the heading risk factors in our annual report
[00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.480]   on Form 20F.
[00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:42.140]   All information in this presentation is as of the date of the presentation.
[00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:46.320]   We undertake no obligation to update or revise any forward-looking statements as a result
[00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:51.100]   of new information, future events, or otherwise, except as required by law.
[00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:55.220]   In addition, today's presentation includes information regarding certain non-GA financial
[00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:56.080]   measures.
[00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:59.680]   Please see the reconciliations of non-GA financial measures attached in today's slide
[00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:00.680]   presentation.
[00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:02.900]   We supplement our IFRS disclosures.
[00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:06.640]   I would now like to hand the call over to Jean-Marc.
[00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:07.640]   Thanks, Ryan.
[00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:12.260]   Good morning, good afternoon, everyone, and thank you for your interest in Constelion.
[00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:14.580]   Let's turn to slide five.
[00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:19.960]   At Constelion, the health and safety of our employees is our first priority.
[00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:26.060]   We have implemented many initiatives to protect our employees in response to the COVID-19
[00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:27.080]   clinic.
[00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:32.240]   We have provided our personnel with personal protective equipment, increased cleaning and
[00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:38.820]   sanitation, allowed for and enforced social distancing, and worked to raise awareness
[00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:40.820]   with our employees.
[00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:45.600]   I want to personally thank our employees for taking this seriously and following the
[00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:48.160]   precautions we have put into place.
[00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:54.340]   As of last Friday, approximately one-half of 1% of our employees have tested positive
[00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.040]   for COVID-19.
[00:02:56.040 --> 00:03:00.280]   And all of whom have recovered, or are recovering.
[00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:04.900]   Needless to say, we must remain vigilant.
[00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:10.180]   During the second quarter, our plans operated well, despite the significant disruptions
[00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:15.160]   to customer demand from lockdowns in both Europe and the U.S.
[00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:19.920]   As I'm speaking, all our plans are running, now and well.
[00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:26.020]   We are carefully monitoring COVID-19 hotspots, both for the health of our employees and any
[00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:29.580]   potential impacts on supply chains.
[00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:34.560]   The demand for our products gradually increased during the course of the second quarter,
[00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:37.280]   and this trend has continued into July.
[00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:44.840]   However, both levels of demand and visibility from our customers remain below historical
[00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:45.840]   levels.
[00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:51.680]   We took strong actions to combat the effects of the pandemic on our business.
